      "writtenOn": "2017-04-25T10:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given none of this is synchronized and the mUrlConnectionFactory (unlike the OkHttpClient) is shared, this seems non-threadsafe.\n\nYou may want to pass the socket factory as an argument to openConnection() or find a different lifecycle model for the factory object. The former is probably easier.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "38791540a961f89dc5aa004f46e8607817482afd",
